{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966806,"nonce":"iPbTYvx2t26xlY+IUr42YgkSGTA=","title":"cn::tree_view expand animation freezes mid-flight, leaving only some children rendered","message":"Click the chevron on a tree node with collapsed children. Visible result:\n\n1. The clicked node's row updates (chevron → \"v\").\n2. The children container appears to be open in layout (subsequent sibling rows are pushed down to their final positions), BUT\n3. Only the first 1–2 children are visible inside it. The rest of the children, and the `overflow_clip` boundary, are frozen at some intermediate animated height.\n4. The frozen state persists indefinitely (~1 second+ in the recording from 2026-05-20).\n5. Any mouse-move or other input event triggers a single redraw that snaps the container to its final fully-expanded state in one frame. There is never a visible animation transition.\n\nSidebar's `animate_bounds(::all().snappy())` plays correctly under the same conditions, so the FLIP/visual-animation system is healthy in general — the bug is specific to the tree.\n\n\n1. **Always render `children_container` with `h(0)` when collapsed** — gave FLIP a stable element for `previous_visual_bounds`. Did not help.\n2. **Switch container animation from `::height()` to `::all().snappy()`** then back. No change.\n3. **`indent_size` 4 → 16 → 8 + guide-line offset fix** — visual-only, unrelated.\n4. **Mirror accordion's collapse pattern**: `.w_full()` always set + `.h(0.0).px(1.0)` when collapsed (vs pure `.h(0.0)`). The `px(1.0)` keeps cross-axis size stable across states. Did not help.\n5. **Compositor fast-path bail** ([windowed.rs:5628](../../crates/blinc_app/src/windowed.rs#L5628)) — added `bounds_anim_active = has_active_visual_animations() || has_active_layout_animations() || has_active_flip_animations()` to the fast-path eligibility check, so fast path can't blit a cached partial-state frame while a bounds animation is mid-flight. This was the leading hypothesis from frame-by-frame video analysis (frames 5–9 showed identical frozen state; frame 10 after a mouse-move snapped to full). Did NOT resolve the symptom.\n\n\n- **Sidebar**: single `animate_bounds` on an outer container that always exists, width animates. Works.\n- **Accordion**: `animate_bounds` on a per-item `collapsible_content` div, height animates between 0 and natural. Works.\n- **Tree**: `animate_bounds` on `children_container` per-node, RECURSIVELY nested inside other `children_container`s, height animates between 0 and natural. Every level of the tree has its own `animate_bounds` config registered. **Doesn't work.**\n\nThe leading remaining hypothesis is that nested visual_animation configs interact badly — possibly the parent's clip rect / animation offset isn't being propagated to deeply-nested children when the parent is the only one with an active animation. Or `compute_animated_render_bounds` isn't being re-run each frame the spring advances. But neither has been confirmed.\n\n\nWhen picking this up: **do not** repeat the failed attempts above. Start with instrumentation:\n\n- Enable `RUST_LOG=blinc_app::redraw_signals=trace,blinc_layout::visual_animation=trace` while clicking to expand a tree node. Confirm whether `visual` shows up in the redraw chain log between click and mouse-move, and whether `update_visual_animations` is being called on frames 2..N.\n- If chain logs say `visual=true` continuously but the children still don't paint, the bug is in `compute_animated_render_bounds` or the walker's clip-application for nested animated bounds. Compare what `get_render_bounds` returns for the `children_container` vs the children inside it across frames.\n- If chain logs show `visual=true` once then drops to false, the spring is settling too early OR `has_active_visible_visual_animations` is failing the `painted.contains(node)` check. Print the painted set for the container's node_id.\n- If chain never fires at all, the issue is upstream of the redraw chain (frame_dirty, wake_proxy, etc.).\n\nRecording at `/Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/Blinc/Screen Recording 2026-05-20 at 12.08.18.mov` shows the exact symptom.\n\n\n`cn::tree_view()` still functions correctly — the layout is always in the right final state after a click. Only the animated reveal is broken. If you don't need the smooth expand, no user action required. To make it appear less broken, you could remove the `animate_bounds` on `children_container` so clicks just snap.","files":null}]}